# Docker build context = repo root, and the repo is ~12 GB (datasets, training
# runs, site render assets). Without this the Pi tars all of it to the daemon on
# every build. The image needs almost nothing from the repo: ros2_ws is
# bind-mounted at run time (see docker/run_pi.sh), so only the HailoRT wheel in
# docker/ actually has to be in context.
#
# NOTE: .dockerignore matches whole paths with filepath.Match — a bare `build/`
# excludes ONLY a top-level build/. Nested paths need `**/`. Getting this wrong
# is silent: the build still works, it just ships 195 MB it didn't need to.

.git/
.swarm/

# Build/runtime artifacts — `**/` so ros2_ws/build, ros2_ws/install, ros2_ws/log
# are actually caught (they are 154 MB / 31 MB / 9.8 MB respectively).
**/build/
**/install/
**/log/
**/runs/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ros2_ws is bind-mounted at run time, so the image never needs it in context.
ros2_ws/

# Model training — 8.8 GB of datasets and weights
training/

# Website — nothing to do with the companion stack
site-v3/

# Sim + docs
sim/results/
docs/
